                <pb facs="0569" n="481" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg481"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Señor de Aspíoz to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of Mexico</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-12-13"><hi rendition="#italic">December 13,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 82.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Most Excellent Sir</hi>: In answer to the note of
                    your Department, No. 543, of the 9th instant, I have the honor to say to you
                    that I have received instructions from my Government to accept the sum of $500
                    in final settlement and full payment of the claim of the Mexican, Eulogio
                    Zambrano, for damages and denial of justice.</p>
                <p>I communicate this for your information and beg you to accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">M. de Azpíroz.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
